			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Simplify payload construction and comment formatting for Webview effects\n\nRefactor the JSON payload creation logic in `Source/Track/Effect/CreateEffectForRequest/Webview.rs` to remove redundant line breaks and align comment formatting. The changes streamline the code structure without altering functional behavior, ensuring positional `args` are correctly mapped to named aliases (`viewId`, `viewType`, `title`) for `SkyBridge` consumption.\n\nThis cleanup maintains consistency with existing IPC strategies and improves code readability while preserving the strict PascalCase naming and positional-to-named argument mapping required for Webview effects.",
			"SHA": "02b66d43bfad2da768c0cbb0f50c6e16f560dc14"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-04T10:41:40Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⣿⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				11
			],
			"Message": "chore(Element): Synchronize 11 submodules to restore debuggability and fix critical IPC payloads\n\nUpdate 11 Element submodules to reverse aggressive minification strategies and address a critical bug in the native backend. Cocoon, Output, Wind, and Worker restore full source map generation, revert single-character variable obfuscation, and reformat ESBuild configurations to strict PascalCase naming, ensuring production builds remain debuggable and maintainable. Mountain fixes the `registerView` payload shape to include the required `viewId` key, restoring functionality for extension sidebars that were previously dropping host content. Maintain adds recursive JSON array deduplication to ensure build idempotency. Rest standardizes CLI quote usage and import ordering. This synchronization prioritizes developer tooling stability and corrects silent failures in the IPC layer.",
			"SHA": "4f0036c738a9dc573ed502230b1e030677a05331"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-03T13:37:41Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⠁⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				6
			],
			"Message": "chore(Element): Synchronize 6 submodules for build normalization and release optimization\n\nUpdate six Element submodules to resolve build pipeline inconsistencies, enforce strict PascalCase naming conventions, and optimize production artifacts.\n\nCocoon and Wind refactor ESBuild configurations into modular structures before applying aggressive minification (removing source maps and renaming to single-char identifiers) for release size reduction, while restoring readable, debuggable builds for development. Output follows suit, reformatting its plugin pipeline for readability before minifying entry points and deleting source maps. Rest standardizes its CLI wrapper with consistent quote usage and import ordering. Worker corrects a deviation by reverting inadvertently minified build scripts to readable PascalCase format. Mountain adds native macOS `dmg` target support, EULA templates, and updated icon assets for the release cycle.\n\nThese changes ensure the editor's build system adheres to project readability standards in development while delivering optimized, deterministic artifacts for production, alongside expanded native distribution capabilities.",
			"SHA": "a0be5a80e41e53753b558beec8107a25ea44b838"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
